# Record the robot's CURRENT map pose under a human-readable name.
#
# Takes no coordinates by design: the operator drives the robot to the spot and
# names it, so a saved location is by construction somewhere the robot has
# physically stood and been localised. Accepting arbitrary coordinates would
# happily record a point inside a wall.
#
# Saving an existing name OVERWRITES it — that is the intended way to nudge a
# destination after re-mapping.
string name
---
bool success
string message
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose   # what was actually stored
